{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Great Places to Visit", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Galapagos Islands", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Wining and Dining > Complaint: What's in My Spinach?", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 15, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Present Perfect Tense vs. The Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way. <br><br>You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event <span class=\"strong\">not</span> necessarily connected to the present.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<ul><li>You can use the Present Perfect tense to talk about experience.</li><li> When you use the Present Perfect tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now. </li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>For example: </li><li><span class=\"italic\">I have eaten lunch.</span> = I ate lunch and now I am not hungry.</li><li><span class=\"italic\">He has bought a painting</span> = He bought the painting in the past and now he has a painting. </li><br><li>Look at the chart about how to form the Present Perfect tense:</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We use <span class=\"strong\"> have/has + the past participle</span>  of the verb in Present Perfect sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past tense form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past participle form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"shelter\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sheltered\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sheltered\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The Islands have sheltered wildlife.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"become\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"became\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"become\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They have become the final destination for many animals.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "The Galapagos Islands have sheltered incredible wildlife for millions of years. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It all began 3 million years ago.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Quantifiers", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use a quantifier before a noun to indicate the amount or number of an item. Quantifiers do not indicate a specific quantity but rather a general amount.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<ul><li>You use quantifiers with both count and non-count nouns.</li><li>Quantifiers like a <span class=\"italic\">a few, several, many, hundreds, thousands</span>, or  <span class=\"italic\">millions</span>, can only be used with count nouns.</li><li>You can use all of the quantifiers below with both count and non-count nouns.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Quantifier\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more<br><br> less/fewer<br><br> no/none<br><br> any /not any<br><br> some<br><br> a lot of / lots of<br><br> plenty of <br><br> enough\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a larger number/amount <br><br> a smaller number/amount<br><br> zero, nothing<br><br> ask about a number or amount/say there is no<br><br> a small number/amount<br><br> a very large number/amount<br><br> more than you need<br><br> as much as you need\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Wind currents led many insects to the islands. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Several types of sea birds made their way to the Galapagos Islands.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to shelter ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to protect or shield from danger ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The islands have sheltered many animals.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le15ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear about natural wonders.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "wildlife ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "animals and plants found in their native habitats", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: The Galapagos Islands are home to a diverse selection of wildlife.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le15ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ancestor ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an early type of animal from which others have evolved ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: How did their ancestors arrive on the islands?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le15ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "current ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the strong motion of water or air ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Wind currents led many insects to the islands.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le15ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to glide ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to move in a smooth, continuous motion ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sea birds glided over long distances to get to the islands", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le15ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "species", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a group of living organisms that share similar features ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Many species found their way to the Galapagos.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le15ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "raft ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a floating platform made of wood or other materials ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Many species traveled on natural rafts.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le15ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "phenomenon ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an observable fact or situation difficult to explain ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Galapagos Islands have become a unique place on earth thanks to natural phenomena.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le15ob01aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le15ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online and find information about a natural wonder. Is it an island? A mountain? A a lake?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a text about this place (12-14 lines).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Give some important facts about its history, the wildlife and its situation today.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your article with your partner and read your partner's article.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research natural wonders.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about natural wonders.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about past events.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"id": 2, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "", "id": 0, "text": "Have you heard of the Galapagos Islands? <br><br>The Galapagos Islands have sheltered incredible wildlife for millions of years. <br>\nWhere did these animals come from? How did their ancestors arrive on the islands?", "time": "100"}, {"image": "", "id": 1, "text": "It all began about 3 million years ago. Wind currents led many insects to the islands. Gulls and several other types of sea birds made their way there with their ability to glide over long distances.<br>\nSea lions and penguins swam there, with the help of the strong currents of the oceans.<br>\nMany other species arrived traveling on natural rafts, which originated along South American riverbanks.<br>\nIn fact, scientists believe that's how the famed Galapagos tortoises got there!<br>", "time": "12500"}, {"image": "", "id": 2, "text": "So, thanks to the wind and the sea and other natural phenomena, the Galapagos have become the final destination for the spiny-crested marine iguana, the lava lizard, the frigate bird, the pintail duck, and thousands of other species that have made the islands their home.", "time": "40000"}], "video_src": "engenn6le15ob01re2vid01"}, "type": "video"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "video", "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "img_path": "", "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about natural wonders. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can discuss experiences I've had or haven't had. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about general and specific quantities.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"